{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118294","id":3501301663,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7QsZ-f","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118294","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118294.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118294.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118294","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118294/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118294/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118294/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6443c2640cb2ef1fb6add9475743b4b4f34b4d6a","number":118294,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix Visual Profiler cursor not appearing when graph is partially filled","user":{"login":"XpolioN2005","id":146839835,"node_id":"U_kgDOCMCZGw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146839835?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005","html_url":"https://github.com/XpolioN2005","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XpolioN2005/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fix Visual Profiler cursor not appearing when graph is partially filled\r\n\r\n### Issue\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118279\r\n\r\nWhen the Visual Profiler graph is not fully filled, clicking does not show the cursor (vertical line). The cursor appears stuck at the left edge.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Cause\r\n\r\nThe issue was caused by arithmetic involving mixed numeric types.\r\n\r\nframe_metrics[last_metric].frame_number is uint64_t, while max_frames is int. When frame_metrics[last_metric].frame_number is smaller than max_frames, the subtraction produces an incorrect value. This leads to a negative frame index after further calculation, which gets clamped to 0, causing the cursor to appear stuck at the left edge.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Fix\r\n\r\nCast frame_metrics[last_metric].frame_number to int64_t before performing the subtraction:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nint64_t first_visible_frame = static_cast<int64_t>(frame_metrics[last_metric].frame_number) - max_frames + 1;\r\nint frame = cursor_metric_edit->get_value() - first_visible_frame;\r\n````\r\n\r\nThis ensures correct frame index calculation and proper cursor positioning when the graph is not fully filled.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Notes\r\n\r\nAI-assisted: Used an LLM for initial understanding of the issue. Final solution was validated and refined manually.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"